diagnosis_text:
Affected component: The firewall (iptables/netfilter) on router6, specifically the FORWARD chain.

Mechanism: Traffic from the rest of the campus toward the “other group” subnets behind router6 arrives on router6’s upstream interface eth2 (10.50.1.2). Router6 has explicit DROP rules on the FORWARD chain for any packets with in-interface eth2, allowing only one narrow exception. As a result, ICMP and all non-exempt traffic from your group are dropped at router6 and never reach the 172.18.51.0/24 hosts, making it look like you’re “banned.”

Localization: Router6 (interfaces eth2 -> eth0/eth1). Evidence:
- Your group hosts (e.g., laptop0 172.16.20.10) can ping 192.168.200.11 but time out to 172.18.51.15/16/17/18. Route
